    "symbol_resolution_caveat": "Addresses were disassembled in the exact stripped measured binaries; symbol names came from same-source, same-LTO symbolized rebuilds whose __text sizes differ from measured binaries by 128 bytes (thin) and 44 bytes (fat), so helper-level names are approximate."
  },
  "interpretation": {
    "finding": "Indirect-control-flow samples land at compiled indirect branch instructions in both LTO variants. Thin Richards samples concentrate at interpreter opcode dispatch; fat samples concentrate mostly at an enum dispatch in object_data_mut, with a smaller interpreter-dispatch cluster.",
    "cycle_gap_explained": false,
    "reason": "These are weighted location samples from one bounded capture per build/workload, not complete event totals or normalized rates. Counts cannot establish that fat has a higher indirect-branch misprediction rate.",
    "l1d": "The local-store load/store sample counts are similar across builds. Richards has more TLB-location samples in the fat capture, but without an event-rate denominator this cannot establish that TLB misses caused the cycle difference. Cache latency remains unresolved.",
    "decision": "Keep the thin-LTO M4 working policy on the matched cycle and diagnostic Score evidence; this PMU result does not justify a dispatch-layout compiler flag or a new optimization."
  },
